    {
      "type": "Feature",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Entrance point to Trail 1 (Dino Trail)",
        "category": "general",
        "info": "\u003Cp\u003E\nTrail 1, also known as the Dino Trail, is a kid-friendly ¼-mile loop. Young explorers can spot dinosaur footprints, play pieces, and other prehistoric-themed equipment along the way.\n\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\n*Please note, ticks and poison ivy are common throughout wooded areas. To keep your walk enjoyable and safe, stick to marked trails, and avoid dense undergrowth or tall grass. When your outing is finished, be sure to thoroughly check yourself, children, and pets for ticks, and wash any exposed skin with cold, soapy water.\n\u003C/p\u003E",
        "url": null,
        "icon": "dino.svg"
      },
      "geometry": {
        "type": "Point",
        "coordinates": [-73.7000079076923, 40.8608662832532]
      }
    },
