    {
      "type": "Feature",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Hempstead House",
        "category": "building",
        "info": "Designed by architects Hunt &amp; Hunt in 1912, this 50,000-square-foot, three-story\nmansion has 40 rooms and a 60-foot-tall entry foyer. It served as the Guggenheims’ summer\nresidence (1917-1942) and the Naval Training Device Center’s dormitories and laboratories\n(1946-1967). Today, visitors can attend a range of cultural events in Hempstead House\nincluding concerts, multi-cultural holiday celebrations, Princess Days at the Castle, history\ntours, and galas. Tours are offered on select Wednesdays and Sundays throughout the year.\nPlease check our calendar for specific event dates. Visit \u003Ca href=\"https://www.sandspointpreserveconservancy.org/about/hempstead-house/\"\u003EHempstead House\u003C/a\u003E for more information.",
        "url": null,
        "icon": null
      },
